Urgency: medium
Maintainer: edulution.io <info@edulution.io>
Changed-By: edulution.io <info@edulution.io>
Description:
 edulution-fileproxy - WebDAV server with SMB backend and NTLM authentication
Changes:
 edulution-fileproxy (1.6.1) noble; urgency=medium
 .
   * The upgrade hands the service user a TLS certificate and key that
     config.yml names elsewhere under /etc/edulution-fileproxy, in a
     directory the service can enter, also on an upgrade from 1.6.0. 1.6.0
     handed over only webdav.key, so a pair kept in a subdirectory such as
     ssl/ stopped the start. For any other pair, such as certbot's, the
     upgrade prints commands that copy it where the service can read it.
   * A file postinst cannot hand over, as on a read-only mount, is reported
     instead of leaving the package unconfigured.
   * The warning an upgrade prints for a configuration the service refuses
     links the documentation of each item, and its check no longer waits
     forever on a FIFO that config.yml names.
